<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battles of Saratoga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1777">1777</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battles of Saratoga were two battles fought near Saratoga, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, in September and October 1777, in which American forces under Horatio Gates defeated a British army advancing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> under John Burgoyne. Burgoyne's surrender on 17 October was a turning point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a>, persuading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to enter into an alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1778.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battles-of-saratoga.jpg" alt="Battles of Saratoga" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Trumbull · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surrender_of_General_Burgoyne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Continental Army under George Washington, aided from 1778 by an alliance with France, won independence despite repeated defeats; the surrender of British armies at <b>Saratoga</b> in 1777 and Yorktown in 1781 proved decisive.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-states">United States · Military</a></li></ul></section>
